M1-MSHA-V1-V2-OPERATOR-REFINEMENT-20261026,20261026,Early gate v1 full15 checkpoint SHA256 e38d18fe...1811 as operator parent; protected M1 as reference,git HEAD 09f3d57c0761b01de1fa3aa29ff296c20ea5e9e9; design-only report and registry revision; existing worktree dirty; no model code changes,No model config; design refinement only,42,Existing LasHeR sequence attribution and train-side fixed-state assets; no new samples,Formula and validation-chain design only; no model execution,NA,NA,NA,NA,NA,NA,NA,Offline documentation review; no GPU process,0,Early gate full15 checkpoint SHA256 e38d18fe50c2895e75e4b9392bf22d9323bb8e6ad31ccbe39ad8c038e3fc1811; no new checkpoint,Test whether full search-distribution co-support can reallocate foreground template Value sources more selectively than independent max-derived direction scaling,"FCSV-R revised to a foreground-source simplex: q=softmax(log pi+alpha*z), g=q/pi, and sum(pi*g)=1 preserves only foreground prior coefficient mass. The operator does not directly reweight Q/K or attention and does not alter same-layer self-Value, CENTER or template update. Actual message norm is not conserved and must be measured; common background can still create false agreement. Existing hard 3x3 cross-QK support did not beat shifted windows, but is a different intervention. No mechanism or performance claim.",OPERATOR-DESIGN-REFINED / MECHANISM-SCREEN-NOT-RUN / NO-TRAINING,experiments/reports/m1_dcvr_v1_v2_value_source_reallocation_20261026.md; experiments/reports/m1_msha_v1_v2_operator_refinement_20261026.md; experiments/reports/m1_early_gate_sequence_scene_attribution_20261026.md,"Next: on the Early gate full15 checkpoint, compare original v1, same-checkpoint gate-bypass native, correct co-support, and shifted co-support at fixed train-side states. First verify same-process tensor repeatability and alpha=0 parity. Stop if correct support does not beat shifted support or if localization change is explained only by total message norm. No training or inference performed."
